unts the omitted one-AND traces and the internal ANDs with no OR-only path to the output. The first child supplies the normalization. The second rules out at most three omitted edges or at most one internal AND. Both have Lean proofs.\n\nThe remaining child starts with four or more omitted edges and two or more internal ANDs. The project checker accepted the exact three-child reduction locally.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/7800/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5655","id":6580331080,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRhd4cw","number":5655,"title":"Reduce L-meta-2590 to three fixed first-gate searches","user":{"login":"psosnin","id":65794094,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1Nzk0MDk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65794094?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin","html_url":"https://github.com/psosnin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/psosnin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T11:03:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T12:20:11Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T12:20:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/5655","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5655","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5655.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5655.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Reduces the Petersen monotone-circuit bound to three explicit 18-gate searches. Their extra input is AND(0,1), OR(0,1), or OR(0,2). Each search uses the 15 minimal positive rows and the 15 maximal negative rows.\n\nA checked table relabels every possible first gate, including repeated, missing, and out-of-range operands. Substitution and constant folding preserve the gate budget for nonconstant outputs. The nonedge AND case is discharged inside the proof. It is false on every minimal positive row, and forcing it to false can only decrease the negative outputs.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5655/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/4921","id":6578763479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRgMaWw","number":4921,"title":"R-meta-2590-704: Normalize Petersen circuits to sets of 30-row truth columns","user":{"login":"wtho704","id":119910905,"node_id":"U_kgDOByWx-Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119910905?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704","html_url":"https://github.com/wtho704","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wtho704/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T09:31:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T15:26:14Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T15:26:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/4921","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/4921","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/4921.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/4921.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Reduce the Petersen monotone circuit lower bound to a finite search on 30 rows. Each wire is identified with the set of rows on which it is true. AND takes an intersection and OR takes a union. The search stores a set of distinct columns, so different wire names, repeated signals, and the order in which independent gates were produced can lead to the same search state.\n\nThe first child proves that this representation works on any finite sample and costs at most one new column per physical gate. It covers constants, gates of fan-in zero or one, and out-of-range wire reads. I have a complete Lean proof of that child. The project verifier accepted it locally against the exact child statement. The second child asks whether the target column can be reached in at most 19 additions. That search remains open.\n\nThe 15 positive rows are edges and the 15 negative rows are maximal independent sets. PR #4786 independently uses these same rows to split the physical circuit by its first gate. This reduction supplies a general normalization theorem and a search over sets of columns. A known 20-gate circuit gives the target on all 1,024 assignments.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/4921/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5121","id":6579200301,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRgi_wg","number":5121,"title":"Reduce L-meta-2590 to an AND gate active on a nonedge and two edges","user":{"login":"jarusoa","id":135768676,"node_id":"U_kgDOCBeqZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135768676?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa","html_url":"https://github.com/jarusoa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarusoa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T09:57:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T12:11:31Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T12:11:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/5121","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5121","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5121.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/5121.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Reduces the 19-gate monotone Petersen circuit question to candidates containing a particular internal AND gate. The gate must be true on the nonedge input {0,2} and on at least two distinct edge inputs. The first child constructs such a candidate at exactly the original size: gates that are true on zero or one edge input can be replaced, and a Petersen symmetry moves the remaining nonedge pair into position. This constructive child has an independent local Lean proof. Excluding the remaining marked circuits is open.\n\nA 21-gate control computes the Petersen edge function on all 1,024 inputs and exhibits this firing pattern. Its marked gate is true on four edge inputs and affects the output.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/5121/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}